Hi Jennifer,

I checked 36 passages against the existing Japanese transcript. Seven lines i=
n the draft need to come back before anything goes to Oakridge; the other 29 =
do not need a translation change. Please keep both the January 27 draft and m=
y marked-up return internal. Neither is ready for Christine.

Please replace Q14, =E2=80=9CAll the conditions were missing from the stop No=
te on screen,=E2=80=9D with =E2=80=9CThe paper had an additional condition. T=
hat part was missing from the stop Note on screen.=E2=80=9D The speaker ident=
ifies that additional part in this Note, not all conditions.

For Q24, please replace =E2=80=9CThe next person completed the processing aft=
er I told them=E2=80=9D with =E2=80=9CThey heard it from me verbally; that is=
 as far as I know. I did not see how they handled it afterward.=E2=80=9D We c=
an report the verbal handoff, but not completion by the next person.

The other returns have different limits: Q02 describes one handoff in the las=
t five shifts, not a daily habit; Q15 says the row exists, although its Note =
alone would not convey everything; and Q19 does not confirm a screen update. =
Q30 describes independent handoffs while allowing that the speaker asks about=
 the source when unsure. Q36 says the paper stayed with the speaker, not that=
 it was submitted to us. My comments identify the corresponding transcript ti=
mes.

Only Q14, Q16 and Q24 have separate permission for their anonymized English t=
ranslations to be used in Christine's report. Please distinguish those three =
from the other candidates in the table; a line needing no translation change =
is not necessarily cleared for external use. The marked-up draft and the full=
 comparison remain for our internal review.

The attached return has the changes and comments; the CSV pairs each passage =
with its checked translation and separates revision from permission. Could yo=
u use these to revise the account before deciding what can go out?

Thanks,
Mihoko

